WEBVTT

00:41.708 --> 00:43.961
NO TAIL TO TELL

00:44.044 --> 00:45.212
Thank you.

00:51.343 --> 00:52.678
Are you asleep already?

01:01.353 --> 01:02.854
She must've been really tired.

01:40.142 --> 01:43.228
Man, what on earth am I thinking?

01:44.563 --> 01:46.440
Hey, wake up.

01:47.107 --> 01:47.983
Hey.

01:49.985 --> 01:50.944
What's this?

01:52.070 --> 01:53.697
Why am I suddenly…

02:21.224 --> 02:23.018
- You!
- What's wrong with you?

02:23.101 --> 02:25.812
Didn't you say you lost
that wooden-handled dagger yesterday?

02:25.896 --> 02:29.066
I didn't lose it. It just wasn't there.

02:29.149 --> 02:31.068
Then why was it in your hand?

02:31.151 --> 02:33.070
What? I told you I don't have it.

02:33.153 --> 02:35.739
I saw it. You just used it to--

02:35.822 --> 02:37.908
Just now? What did I do?

02:39.034 --> 02:40.994
You used it to--

02:41.078 --> 02:43.955
You were dead asleep until a second ago.

02:44.039 --> 02:46.083
Why are you suddenly
rambling about the dagger?

02:46.166 --> 02:48.293
Did you have a weird dream or something?

02:49.086 --> 02:49.961
A dream?

02:50.045 --> 02:52.464
I mean, you just woke up
and started talking nonsense.

02:52.547 --> 02:55.258
It wasn't a dream.
It was more like a prophecy…

02:55.342 --> 02:57.636
No, no… wait a second.

02:58.387 --> 03:00.681
I'm not a nine-tailed fox anymore.
I'm just human.

03:00.764 --> 03:03.934
My spiritual power
and abilities are all gone.

03:04.017 --> 03:05.602
And I suddenly see the future?

03:05.686 --> 03:06.937
That's impossible.

03:08.397 --> 03:10.232
So it really was a dream.

03:11.900 --> 03:13.402
Seriously, what are you doing?

03:14.486 --> 03:16.488
I was scared for a second.

03:17.280 --> 03:19.282
Maybe it's because
I'm running on fumes.

03:20.450 --> 03:22.119
What a crappy dream.

03:22.744 --> 03:24.871
What did you dream about anyway?

03:25.747 --> 03:28.667
None of your business.
I don't even want to think about it.

03:37.718 --> 03:39.553
Dream or not, I'm still pissed.

03:40.220 --> 03:41.680
You've got a lot of nerve.

03:47.769 --> 03:48.854
Oh my.

03:49.813 --> 03:51.565
What's her problem?

03:55.026 --> 03:58.363
She's something else.
A real piece of work.

04:06.747 --> 04:07.664
Si-yeol!

04:09.082 --> 04:10.959
Wait for me.

04:13.253 --> 04:16.631
OVERNIGHT WITH THE MOON
GUESTHOUSE

04:16.715 --> 04:19.426
You only have one room left?

04:19.968 --> 04:22.095
Don't be ridiculous.

04:22.929 --> 04:25.974
How could that be?
Who'd even stay in a dump like this?

04:26.057 --> 04:29.186
Only a "dump" like this
would even have a room left.

04:29.811 --> 04:31.688
And you came the night
before the long weekend.

04:31.772 --> 04:33.482
Go somewhere else then.

04:34.524 --> 04:36.276
Please give us a moment.

04:36.359 --> 04:37.569
Come with me.

04:39.112 --> 04:41.281
What is it?

04:41.364 --> 04:44.242
We've been looking for hours,
and this is all there is.

04:44.326 --> 04:46.703
What choice do we have?
Sleep on the street?

04:47.496 --> 04:50.165
Why would I need to?
Instead of this dump,

04:50.248 --> 04:52.042
let's go to a five-star hotel.

04:52.125 --> 04:54.795
Jeez, where would we even get the money?

04:54.878 --> 04:57.547
Let's just stay here for the night.

04:58.048 --> 04:59.216
- No.
- Why not?

05:00.217 --> 05:02.886
It's dirty, cramped, and most of all…

05:05.263 --> 05:06.681
it feels sketchy.

05:06.765 --> 05:09.059
What feels sketchy?

05:10.227 --> 05:11.561
What, me?

05:12.813 --> 05:14.356
What are you even thinking?

05:16.691 --> 05:18.610
You must be joking.

05:18.693 --> 05:21.822
You're centuries older than me.
Give me a break.

05:21.905 --> 05:24.491
- No, it's not that.
- Then what?

05:25.158 --> 05:26.284
It's…

05:31.164 --> 05:32.374
It's just that earlier…

05:36.920 --> 05:38.505
Fine. Let's take it.

05:38.588 --> 05:41.049
I just had a bad dream,
but it's probably nothing.

05:41.550 --> 05:42.551
Let's go.

05:46.179 --> 05:47.889
Seriously, what is wrong with her?

06:05.824 --> 06:08.410
Why did I suddenly have a dream like that?

06:10.704 --> 06:15.709
With the way Si-yeol picks on me,
no wonder I'm having dreams like that.

06:15.792 --> 06:17.043
Jeez.

06:21.172 --> 06:23.508
What… is that?

06:24.259 --> 06:26.052
What? This?

06:26.136 --> 06:29.598
What are you going to do with that?
Get back at me or something?

06:30.807 --> 06:31.850
What are you talking about?

06:33.351 --> 06:35.979
The owner brought this over
so we could have some fruit.

06:40.442 --> 06:42.527
Oh, really?

06:45.989 --> 06:46.948
Oh boy.

06:52.120 --> 06:54.080
I guess you do have a shred of conscience.

06:55.373 --> 06:56.374
What?

06:56.458 --> 06:59.169
I don't know what you dreamed about,

06:59.252 --> 07:03.298
but it's probably just guilt
over how you treated me.

07:03.798 --> 07:04.799
That's not it.

07:05.634 --> 07:07.093
Sure it is.

07:07.969 --> 07:11.139
See? Guilt always catches up with you.

07:12.849 --> 07:16.186
If it's bothering you,
I guess you really are human after all.

07:21.733 --> 07:22.651
Here.

07:26.988 --> 07:29.032
Could that be it?

07:30.158 --> 07:32.744
Being human is such a hassle.

07:36.206 --> 07:38.083
I've lost my appetite.

07:42.921 --> 07:45.715
Oh my gosh.

07:46.758 --> 07:49.260
Do you really think you're up
for another hike tomorrow?

07:49.344 --> 07:51.137
I don't know.

07:59.229 --> 08:00.313
What is that?

08:00.814 --> 08:02.190
Stay still.

08:03.817 --> 08:05.610
That's part of being human.

08:06.236 --> 08:08.822
You get sore when you use muscles
you don't normally use.

08:08.905 --> 08:10.365
You'll get used to it.

08:11.741 --> 08:12.742
I won't need to.

08:13.410 --> 08:15.829
I'll do whatever it takes
to get my old life back.

08:20.166 --> 08:21.209
Here too.

08:21.292 --> 08:23.086
Don't hold back. Put plenty on.

08:28.133 --> 08:30.802
- Nice and cool, right?
- Yeah.

08:30.885 --> 08:32.262
The soles too.

08:33.054 --> 08:35.849
Not there, you dummy.

08:35.932 --> 08:39.060
OVERNIGHT WITH THE MOON
GUESTHOUSE

09:38.620 --> 09:39.537
Oh my.

09:42.207 --> 09:43.208
You're still up?

09:44.250 --> 09:46.419
I'm so sore I can't sleep.

09:53.968 --> 09:57.097
What are you doing out here at this hour,
looking all pathetic?

10:00.934 --> 10:03.561
I've always wanted to try this.

10:04.187 --> 10:06.439
Just having a beer like this at night.

10:06.523 --> 10:09.734
I won't be able to do this
once I have my life back.

10:11.736 --> 10:13.947
Why not? Just go for it.

10:15.031 --> 10:16.866
Life's short enough as it is.

10:18.660 --> 10:21.579
You know what the human body's like now.

10:23.414 --> 10:25.583
If you just do whatever you feel like,

10:26.543 --> 10:28.711
you'll never get to do
what you really want.

10:30.588 --> 10:33.967
It's just one beer.
What difference does it make?

10:34.050 --> 10:35.468
A big one.

10:35.552 --> 10:38.346
An athlete's body
is like a finely tuned machine.

10:38.972 --> 10:41.975
Everything you eat,
how often and when you eat,

10:42.058 --> 10:44.352
and even your sleep cycle all matter.

10:44.435 --> 10:46.855
It all shows
when you're out there on the field.

10:47.605 --> 10:49.566
You're so dramatic.

10:52.277 --> 10:54.320
Are all other humans like you?

10:54.404 --> 10:56.447
No. That's why I'm the best in the world.

10:57.615 --> 10:58.533
What?

11:05.790 --> 11:06.666
Give me one.

11:07.292 --> 11:09.627
Since I'm human now, I want to get drunk.

11:13.339 --> 11:15.341
Why have you never had a drink before?

11:16.467 --> 11:19.470
Does alcohol weaken
a nine-tailed fox's spiritual power?

11:19.554 --> 11:20.430
As if.

11:21.264 --> 11:24.058
No matter how much I drank,
I just couldn't get drunk.

11:42.827 --> 11:45.413
Have you ever seen
any other nine-tailed foxes?

11:54.672 --> 11:55.840
That must be lonely.

11:58.718 --> 11:59.636
I have.

12:02.096 --> 12:03.932
So I wasn't really lonely.

12:04.641 --> 12:07.185
It was just the two of us for a long time.

12:08.895 --> 12:10.897
- Then where is…
- She died.

12:12.273 --> 12:13.733
After becoming human.

12:16.110 --> 12:17.028
I see.

12:24.118 --> 12:26.204
So this is what getting drunk feels like.

12:54.607 --> 12:56.442
It's a bit cold at night.

13:00.071 --> 13:04.075
A fragile human,
still trying to act tough.

13:05.702 --> 13:09.414
You seem to keep forgetting,
but you're just a human woman now.

13:18.047 --> 13:20.383
Oh, I get it.

13:20.925 --> 13:24.887
This is like a human male hitting
on a female. It's called flirting.

13:25.388 --> 13:27.390
Flirt… Are you nuts?

13:28.641 --> 13:29.934
Give it back.

13:30.018 --> 13:31.853
- Give me--
- Hey, no take-backs.

13:32.395 --> 13:33.771
It's nice and warm.

13:34.397 --> 13:36.774
Look, let me be clear.

13:37.400 --> 13:39.068
This is not flirting.

13:39.694 --> 13:42.155
It's called manners, okay?

13:43.489 --> 13:45.325
Don't be shy.

13:45.408 --> 13:47.327
With my looks and charm,

13:48.161 --> 13:49.787
of course you'd fall for me.

13:50.413 --> 13:52.540
I am a nine-tailed fox, after all.

13:54.667 --> 13:56.252
You are unbelievable.

13:57.545 --> 13:59.422
Okay. I'll pretend I didn't notice.

13:59.505 --> 14:00.882
Notice what?

14:00.965 --> 14:02.884
I shouldn't have given you the jacket.

14:03.718 --> 14:05.595
It's so warm.

14:12.185 --> 14:14.312
Do you know the name
of that constellation?

14:14.395 --> 14:15.438
No, what is it?

14:15.521 --> 14:17.148
I'm asking because I don't know.

14:17.857 --> 14:18.941
It's pretty.

14:19.734 --> 14:24.113
EPISODE 5
THE CHANGER, THE CHANGED, AND THE LACKING

14:34.248 --> 14:35.291
Woo-seok.

14:37.168 --> 14:39.045
What are you doing up this late?

14:41.422 --> 14:43.341
I just couldn't sleep.

14:44.550 --> 14:46.302
Couldn't sleep? Why?

14:49.597 --> 14:51.891
Because I'm scared.

14:54.394 --> 14:56.187
It feels like when I wake up,

14:57.105 --> 14:59.065
everything will just vanish.

15:00.483 --> 15:02.026
Like a dream.

15:02.819 --> 15:03.945
Like a mirage.

15:15.665 --> 15:18.835
We'd pass as hikers now, right?

15:19.961 --> 15:23.256
Of course. Let's go get stranded.

15:48.239 --> 15:50.116
Why are there so many people here?

15:50.199 --> 15:53.703
The owner said today's the start
of the long weekend.

15:53.786 --> 15:55.746
We won't get stranded
with this many people around.

15:55.830 --> 15:58.875
One small scream,
and people will swarm in to save us.

15:58.958 --> 16:00.084
Coming through.

16:02.295 --> 16:03.212
Seriously.

16:04.046 --> 16:05.047
This isn't going to work.

16:06.090 --> 16:07.925
We need to go somewhere secluded.

16:17.768 --> 16:19.729
Man, I'm dying here.

16:19.812 --> 16:21.147
How much farther?

16:21.230 --> 16:22.440
In my experience,

16:22.523 --> 16:25.401
we'll end up deep in the woods
if we go a little farther.

16:25.485 --> 16:27.820
We can rest there until nightfall.

16:50.551 --> 16:51.427
Are you okay?

16:52.595 --> 16:53.471
What?

16:54.430 --> 16:55.306
Yeah.

18:09.672 --> 18:11.299
I can't take another step.

18:13.426 --> 18:15.303
I think we're officially stranded.

18:15.386 --> 18:17.305
I couldn't find the trail even if I tried.

18:41.412 --> 18:42.663
I'm so sleepy.

18:44.373 --> 18:47.710
You can't sleep out here.
You'll freeze to death.

18:47.793 --> 18:50.254
- Just a little nap.
- Absolutely not.

18:51.797 --> 18:52.923
Hang on.

18:56.218 --> 18:57.345
Try some of this.

18:58.220 --> 18:59.930
It'll wake you up.

19:07.313 --> 19:10.232
Yes, I think it's working.

19:10.316 --> 19:11.817
That's good.

19:18.115 --> 19:19.909
When is she going to show up?

19:20.826 --> 19:22.370
The sun went down ages ago.

19:25.081 --> 19:28.459
Hey, what if…

19:28.542 --> 19:31.629
What if there's no nine-tailed fox here?
What happens to us then?

19:33.339 --> 19:34.256
What?

19:34.965 --> 19:36.008
I mean,

19:36.884 --> 19:38.552
I was just thinking

19:39.136 --> 19:41.305
that the newspaper article
was from 28 years ago.

19:41.389 --> 19:44.308
Maybe she's become a human like you.

19:44.392 --> 19:45.393
No way.

19:47.186 --> 19:49.230
Becoming human isn't that easy.

19:50.773 --> 19:53.484
Considering I didn't even know
there was a nine-tailed fox here,

19:53.567 --> 19:55.861
she can't be more than 300
or 400 years old.

19:57.613 --> 19:59.490
No way she's turned human yet.

20:00.199 --> 20:01.117
Right?

20:01.742 --> 20:02.743
- Yes.
- Yes.

20:04.286 --> 20:05.371
But…

20:08.082 --> 20:09.041
it's freezing.

20:09.750 --> 20:10.710
Yes.

20:14.922 --> 20:16.424
- Should we--
- Should we head back?

20:16.507 --> 20:18.217
- Yeah.
- Okay.

20:18.300 --> 20:20.594
Okay… grab your stuff.

20:24.807 --> 20:27.435
Why do humans have such poor night vision?

20:28.269 --> 20:30.438
I can't see a single thing.

20:30.521 --> 20:33.107
Seriously, where are we?

20:41.782 --> 20:42.700
Oh no.

20:44.076 --> 20:46.245
Can we call those rangers
from yesterday?

20:48.706 --> 20:50.583
I haven't had signal for a while.

20:53.377 --> 20:55.087
Am I really going to die?

20:55.713 --> 20:58.799
Out here? Right after becoming human?

20:58.883 --> 21:00.384
We're not going to die.

21:01.302 --> 21:03.721
I can't die here. I'm Kang Si-yeol.

21:07.516 --> 21:11.437
Si-yeol! Where are you?

21:15.149 --> 21:16.025
Si-yeol!

21:17.943 --> 21:19.236
Si-yeol.

21:21.781 --> 21:23.616
Are you okay? You're not dead, are you?

21:23.699 --> 21:27.453
I'm not dead, but I think I'm done for.

21:28.579 --> 21:29.747
What?

21:29.830 --> 21:31.457
I sprained my ankle.

21:36.545 --> 21:38.798
- Check your phone again.
- Okay.

21:44.970 --> 21:46.096
What?

21:46.180 --> 21:47.306
No!

22:04.448 --> 22:05.783
Do you need help?

22:18.671 --> 22:19.630
Geum-ho?

22:33.352 --> 22:34.812
Is it really you?

22:36.522 --> 22:37.898
How can you be…

22:40.025 --> 22:43.571
All this time, I thought you were dead…

22:50.786 --> 22:52.997
Hey, what's wrong with you?

22:56.333 --> 22:57.459
Do you know me?

23:02.965 --> 23:04.300
What?

23:04.383 --> 23:05.718
How do you know me?

23:17.146 --> 23:20.274
Right. I forget this is what they do.

23:20.816 --> 23:22.818
I was being naive.

23:23.402 --> 23:25.988
You can't be Geum-ho.

23:26.655 --> 23:29.742
She became human and died of old age.

23:33.329 --> 23:35.956
What kind of sick joke is this?

23:38.459 --> 23:40.210
Did I do something wrong?

23:41.837 --> 23:45.883
Are you pretending not to know,
or do you really not know anything?

23:49.470 --> 23:51.347
Just who the hell are you?

23:53.140 --> 23:54.308
Well…

23:56.101 --> 23:58.437
I'm just a fox cultivating myself
in the mountains.

24:03.233 --> 24:04.693
Right. Of course.

24:04.777 --> 24:07.529
This must be the will of Heaven.

24:09.073 --> 24:12.159
And I'm just the fool dancing to the tune.

24:13.911 --> 24:15.704
Hey, where are you going?

24:16.330 --> 24:17.623
Don't follow me!

24:18.832 --> 24:20.584
It's dangerous that way.

24:21.210 --> 24:22.795
That's not a trail humans use.

24:23.379 --> 24:26.173
She said it's dangerous.
What's wrong with you?

24:28.717 --> 24:30.427
I told you not to follow me.

24:33.555 --> 24:35.516
Hey! You--

24:37.226 --> 24:38.477
That little…

25:12.928 --> 25:16.181
Show yourself. I know you're watching!

25:18.392 --> 25:20.310
Come out right now!

25:23.814 --> 25:27.026
Stop hiding like a coward and face me!

25:30.529 --> 25:32.448
Why do I have to be human?

25:33.532 --> 25:37.828
And why is a nine-tailed fox that looks
just like Geum-ho showing up now?

25:37.911 --> 25:40.080
Who the hell is she?

25:40.164 --> 25:42.458
What do you want from me?

25:52.968 --> 25:54.428
What are you doing?

25:54.511 --> 25:56.430
I sprained my ankle earlier.

25:56.513 --> 25:59.016
I need to catch up to her fast.

26:04.980 --> 26:06.106
It should feel better now.

26:15.115 --> 26:16.408
Is this fun for you?

26:16.492 --> 26:18.911
Treating me like your toy?

26:20.454 --> 26:21.747
Right.

26:22.289 --> 26:25.751
I bet I'm just a pawn on your chessboard.

26:27.086 --> 26:32.174
Setting up all these schemes
and messing with someone's fate

26:32.257 --> 26:34.259
is just how you do things.

26:44.061 --> 26:48.649
But you know,
I've got my own way of doing things.

26:49.566 --> 26:52.778
I just ignore everything you say
and do whatever the hell I want.

26:53.362 --> 26:54.488
You already knew that.

26:55.114 --> 26:58.617
I don't know why you turned me human
or what you want from me,

26:58.700 --> 27:02.621
and I don't even know why you sent
someone who looks just like Geum-ho.

27:03.705 --> 27:07.000
But whatever your plan is,
I'm not playing along.

27:08.627 --> 27:11.505
I'll fight back with everything I've got.

27:18.637 --> 27:19.888
Hey!

27:22.641 --> 27:23.642
Hey.

27:25.894 --> 27:27.187
Are you okay?

27:27.271 --> 27:28.647
Yeah.

27:30.274 --> 27:33.235
You scared me. Seriously, you're…

27:34.862 --> 27:36.071
It's cold out.

27:39.825 --> 27:40.909
Hey, you.

27:41.869 --> 27:43.078
Go start a fire or something.

27:45.539 --> 27:46.623
Excuse me?

27:59.428 --> 28:02.055
- Got anything to eat?
- Oh! Just a moment.

28:10.606 --> 28:12.107
What was that about earlier?

28:12.941 --> 28:15.277
Nothing. Just a misunderstanding.

28:16.195 --> 28:17.487
A misunderstanding?

28:18.488 --> 28:21.200
You made a scene like that
over a misunderstanding?

28:21.700 --> 28:22.910
That's right.

28:22.993 --> 28:24.411
Oh, come on.

28:24.494 --> 28:27.247
That was way too dramatic.

28:27.331 --> 28:29.958
If that nine-tailed fox
had a nasty temper like yours,

28:30.042 --> 28:31.960
we'd be dead by now.

28:32.044 --> 28:33.462
What's wrong with my temper?

28:33.545 --> 28:36.924
I'm just saying we're the ones
who need help right now.

28:37.007 --> 28:39.259
Why pick a fight
when we should be sucking up to her?

28:39.343 --> 28:41.803
You're the one
who needs to suck up to her, not me.

28:41.887 --> 28:43.889
And I didn't start the fight.

28:43.972 --> 28:46.391
The ones above are
picking a fight with me.

28:47.476 --> 28:49.019
What are you talking about?

28:50.187 --> 28:51.772
I told you last night.

28:52.606 --> 28:56.318
There was another nine-tailed fox
that I lived with for a very long time.

28:57.027 --> 28:57.903
And?

28:59.821 --> 29:02.157
That fox is the spitting image of her.

29:03.075 --> 29:06.453
I knew her for centuries,
and yet even I was fooled for a moment.

29:08.747 --> 29:11.541
Right after I become human,

29:11.625 --> 29:14.670
I run into a fox
who looks exactly like her.

29:15.545 --> 29:19.049
That's no coincidence.
They must be up to something.

29:23.178 --> 29:25.973
It feels like they're just
openly toying with me,

29:26.056 --> 29:27.975
and it pisses me off.

29:30.811 --> 29:31.687
Well,

29:32.729 --> 29:35.232
let's not overcomplicate things.

29:35.857 --> 29:37.067
Keep it simple.

29:38.277 --> 29:40.654
What? How?

29:42.531 --> 29:45.075
Let's solve my problem first.

29:45.826 --> 29:51.790
So even if you're annoyed,
just suck it up and be nice to her.

29:51.873 --> 29:54.876
If she refuses my wish,
are you going to take responsibility?

29:54.960 --> 29:57.170
- You little--
- Hey…

29:57.796 --> 29:59.631
Here, have some of this.

30:06.013 --> 30:07.431
What is this?

30:07.931 --> 30:11.101
This is Fischer's ragwort, that's mugwort,

30:11.184 --> 30:13.395
wild chives, spring cabbage,

30:13.478 --> 30:15.689
coastal hog fennel, shepherd's purse--

30:15.772 --> 30:17.274
That's not what I mean.

30:18.233 --> 30:21.486
You want us to eat this raw?

30:22.279 --> 30:24.323
I washed them in the stream.

30:24.906 --> 30:28.660
Gosh, I guess you're a vegetarian.

30:31.747 --> 30:34.750
Is this what you normally live on?

30:34.833 --> 30:36.126
What are you, a goat?

30:37.544 --> 30:38.879
I'm a fox.

30:40.797 --> 30:44.343
I mean, why would a fox
live on just greens?

30:44.426 --> 30:47.929
Did your mountain god say
you can't self-cultivate if you eat meat?

30:48.680 --> 30:52.434
Not really. I mean, I've lived
on this mountain for so long.

30:52.517 --> 30:53.852
So whenever I try to hunt animals,

30:53.935 --> 30:56.688
it turns out I either know them
or know someone who does.

30:56.772 --> 30:58.982
I can't exactly eat my friend's
great-great-granddaughter.

30:59.066 --> 31:00.525
True.

31:01.651 --> 31:04.654
- What?
- Hey, that's not important.

31:05.238 --> 31:07.616
This is great. So fresh.

31:09.034 --> 31:12.454
You know, I eat a ton of salad too.

31:12.537 --> 31:14.790
Look at that!
We have so much in common.

31:15.957 --> 31:17.042
Please, eat up.

31:22.881 --> 31:24.424
All right, enough.

31:24.508 --> 31:26.843
Stop stalling and tell her why we're here.

31:30.055 --> 31:31.723
Right.

31:33.642 --> 31:34.851
The thing is,

31:35.852 --> 31:37.729
we didn't exactly get lost.

31:39.272 --> 31:41.483
We actually came here looking for you.

31:42.651 --> 31:44.903
Looking for me? Why?

31:51.743 --> 31:53.412
Because I have a wish.

32:08.635 --> 32:09.845
What is this?

32:10.637 --> 32:11.805
What's happening?

32:35.996 --> 32:38.540
You can't just do this all of a sudden.

32:38.623 --> 32:40.167
How can you do this?

32:43.378 --> 32:44.379
HYEON WOO-SEOK, MY STORY

33:08.862 --> 33:09.863
What's happening?

33:09.946 --> 33:10.906
It didn't work.

33:12.824 --> 33:13.992
Excuse me?

33:14.075 --> 33:15.911
I just tried, but it didn't work.

33:15.994 --> 33:17.579
Why didn't it work?

33:18.413 --> 33:20.957
Something was just happening!
Why did it stop?

33:21.583 --> 33:24.127
Well, actually, I--

33:24.211 --> 33:25.837
Just how old are you?

33:25.921 --> 33:28.089
How long have you been a nine-tailed fox?

33:29.341 --> 33:31.426
About 500 years.

33:32.385 --> 33:33.762
Then why can't you pull this off?

33:34.804 --> 33:38.266
I've never done anything like this,
so I didn't even know it was possible.

33:38.350 --> 33:40.769
Well, can't you just
teach her how to do it?

33:41.811 --> 33:44.356
- No, I can't.
- Why not?

33:44.439 --> 33:46.274
She doesn't have enough spiritual power.

33:46.358 --> 33:47.943
It's not about technique.

33:49.027 --> 33:51.112
Come on, that makes no sense.

33:51.196 --> 33:53.323
She healed my ankle just fine.

33:53.406 --> 33:55.742
She was teleporting all over the place!

33:55.825 --> 33:57.577
So why can't she do this?

33:58.620 --> 34:02.290
You can't compare a fate-altering spell
to those cheap party tricks.

34:02.374 --> 34:03.500
Jeez.

34:03.583 --> 34:05.585
Beats me why
a 500-year-old nine-tailed fox

34:05.669 --> 34:07.921
has so little spiritual power.

34:09.381 --> 34:11.550
Well, the thing is--

34:11.633 --> 34:15.011
No… no, this can't be real.

34:15.095 --> 34:16.429
Look.

34:17.389 --> 34:19.349
Just try it one more time. Please.

34:20.016 --> 34:21.977
Maybe it'll work this time.

34:22.060 --> 34:23.311
Well…

34:23.937 --> 34:26.648
It won't matter how many times she tries.

34:27.274 --> 34:29.609
She lacks power. Were you not listening?

34:30.360 --> 34:33.238
Does this not matter to you?
Whose fault is it that I'm in this mess?

34:33.321 --> 34:35.657
Do I look like I'm having fun right now?

34:35.740 --> 34:37.993
I'm in this mess because of you!

34:38.076 --> 34:39.369
You're blaming me?

34:39.452 --> 34:40.328
Obviously.

34:40.412 --> 34:43.248
I should've just let you die back then.

34:43.331 --> 34:44.583
- Hey!
- What?

34:44.666 --> 34:46.626
Please don't fight--

34:46.710 --> 34:49.421
- This is all your fault.
- What?

34:49.504 --> 34:52.549
You're a nine-tailed fox.
How can you be this useless?

34:52.632 --> 34:55.760
Well, actually, I'm not a nine-tailed fox.

34:57.178 --> 34:59.598
What? Come again?

35:00.640 --> 35:04.519
I kept trying to tell you,
but you kept cutting me off.

35:05.270 --> 35:08.523
What? Then what are you?

35:09.816 --> 35:12.527
I'm not a nine-tailed fox.

35:13.153 --> 35:14.654
I'm an eight-tailed fox.

35:14.738 --> 35:16.072
Eight tails.

35:20.869 --> 35:22.203
What?

35:31.838 --> 35:32.881
CALL
SI-YEOL

35:35.842 --> 35:38.637
The person you are calling is unavailable…

35:38.720 --> 35:41.097
What? Why is his phone off?

35:46.061 --> 35:48.813
What the hell is going on?

35:52.776 --> 35:56.571
Five, six, seven,

35:58.031 --> 35:59.074
eight.

36:00.116 --> 36:01.326
There really are only eight.

36:01.409 --> 36:03.578
I should have known.

36:03.662 --> 36:06.790
No wonder she seemed a bit lacking.

36:08.291 --> 36:10.377
What is an eight-tailed fox anyway?

36:11.044 --> 36:12.921
I've never heard of anything like that.

36:13.004 --> 36:16.591
If a nine-tailed fox has nine tails,
what do you think an eight-tailed fox is?

36:17.133 --> 36:18.510
A fox with eight tails.

36:19.177 --> 36:21.054
You know that's not what I meant.

36:21.971 --> 36:24.349
They all start out pretty much the same.

36:24.432 --> 36:28.186
Just an ordinary fox
who suddenly starts thinking.

36:33.274 --> 36:37.779
"Why are they human,
while I am nothing but a beast?"

36:39.739 --> 36:43.243
"How can I become something more?"

36:45.245 --> 36:49.249
Once a fox reaches that enlightenment
and begins to cultivate themselves,

36:49.332 --> 36:52.961
they start to shed their animal form
and become closer to a human.

36:54.003 --> 36:55.672
For centuries,

36:56.256 --> 36:58.174
as their enlightenment grows,

36:58.800 --> 37:01.720
they gain one tail after another.

37:05.557 --> 37:10.270
So, since she's missing a tail,
she's still more beast than human.

37:10.353 --> 37:13.148
She hasn't trained enough
to be a true nine-tailed fox.

37:14.482 --> 37:17.694
How do you know so much about this?

37:21.364 --> 37:22.741
Because I went through it myself.

37:25.034 --> 37:27.454
All that waiting.
All those years of dreaming.

37:31.082 --> 37:32.125
Pardon?

37:33.501 --> 37:36.546
I was a nine-tailed fox
until just a few days ago.

37:38.047 --> 37:40.508
Though now I'm stuck being human.

37:41.426 --> 37:43.678
Wait, so what happens now?

37:43.762 --> 37:46.431
What about me?
Can't I go back to the way I was?

37:46.514 --> 37:48.349
We'll have to find another way.

37:48.433 --> 37:49.768
Since she's clearly--

37:49.851 --> 37:52.270
It's you. The one I've been waiting for.

37:53.730 --> 37:54.773
What?

37:54.856 --> 37:58.109
I've been waiting for you to come.
For over 200 years, sis.

37:59.819 --> 38:01.196
What are you talking about?

38:01.279 --> 38:04.616
The mountain god told me before he left

38:04.699 --> 38:06.701
that someone would come
to take care of me.

38:07.911 --> 38:09.245
You think that's me?

38:10.121 --> 38:12.707
Yes! Though I didn't think
it'd take 200 years.

38:13.458 --> 38:16.085
Still, since you came all this way--

38:16.920 --> 38:19.214
I think you've got the wrong idea.

38:19.297 --> 38:20.882
Please tell me, sis.

38:20.965 --> 38:23.593
How can I become human like you?

38:25.970 --> 38:27.430
What?

38:33.311 --> 38:35.814
I want to become human
as soon as possible.

38:57.585 --> 38:58.670
Wait.

39:02.549 --> 39:04.300
Where did that nice nine-tailed fox go?

39:05.510 --> 39:07.053
Or was it an eight-tailed fox?

39:07.804 --> 39:08.930
"Nice nine-tailed fox"?

39:09.556 --> 39:11.599
Then am I the bad nine-tailed fox?

39:11.683 --> 39:13.226
Where did she go, anyway?

39:14.310 --> 39:16.354
Who cares? She probably went on her way.

39:17.397 --> 39:19.232
I'm tired. Let's head back down.

39:20.108 --> 39:22.819
Is it all right to just leave
without saying goodbye?

39:23.778 --> 39:26.114
I mean, isn't she your kin or something?

39:26.197 --> 39:28.700
Why say goodbye
when we won't see each other again?

39:30.118 --> 39:32.078
Are you going to stay and live here?

39:33.329 --> 39:35.415
Okay, fine. Let's go.

39:35.498 --> 39:36.791
Man…

39:37.458 --> 39:39.919
Don't go off alone. It's dangerous.

39:40.003 --> 39:41.129
Hurry up.

39:50.805 --> 39:52.807
Are you changing hotels again today?

39:54.726 --> 39:55.977
Damn it.

39:57.228 --> 39:58.479
Yes.

39:59.397 --> 40:00.899
Today's the chairman's birthday.

40:00.982 --> 40:03.276
Shouldn't you at least attend the dinner?

40:04.277 --> 40:07.572
Forget it.
It's not like anyone wants me there.

40:15.705 --> 40:17.916
Did you look into what I asked for?

40:17.999 --> 40:19.876
Well, Mr. Lee.

40:21.044 --> 40:23.212
Is what you're looking for

40:23.296 --> 40:26.049
the name of some organization?

40:26.549 --> 40:28.760
What the hell are you talking about?

40:29.928 --> 40:31.346
I said, the nine-tailed fox.

40:31.971 --> 40:34.891
You know, the fox with nine tails.

40:35.433 --> 40:38.686
Didn't I tell you to find out everything
about the nine-tailed fox?

40:41.689 --> 40:44.400
Mr. Lee, those things aren't real.

40:45.234 --> 40:47.904
What are you talking about? You saw it.

40:48.404 --> 40:49.948
You were right there with me.

40:51.824 --> 40:52.867
I was?

40:54.494 --> 40:58.039
Hey… pull over, you bastard.

41:06.965 --> 41:09.008
Never mind. Just leave.

41:10.802 --> 41:12.011
Mr. Lee--

41:12.804 --> 41:14.263
I said get out.

41:14.347 --> 41:16.641
You probably think I'm crazy too,

41:16.724 --> 41:19.060
and you won't even bother looking into it.

41:19.143 --> 41:21.646
Mr. Lee, if word gets out

41:22.438 --> 41:24.315
that you're looking into such things--

41:24.399 --> 41:28.361
I get it, so please leave
and stop wasting your time on a nutcase.

41:33.950 --> 41:35.702
Hey, wait!

41:38.663 --> 41:41.833
Just… hold on.

41:44.002 --> 41:45.211
Who are you people?

41:45.294 --> 41:47.630
I've seen that bastard somewhere before.

41:51.926 --> 41:53.636
Is he actually dying?

41:57.890 --> 41:58.808
That's it.

41:59.767 --> 42:01.436
I knew he looked familiar.

42:02.520 --> 42:03.396
Secretary Choi.

42:04.355 --> 42:07.650
Look into the records of the car accident
from nine years ago.

42:08.276 --> 42:09.360
Pardon?

42:09.861 --> 42:11.988
The kid I hit with my car.

42:12.071 --> 42:17.368
Find out everything about who he is,
where he lives, and what he's doing.

42:30.131 --> 42:31.257
Hey.

42:31.340 --> 42:35.011
Did you have to be so harsh yesterday?

42:38.139 --> 42:40.641
How can I become human like you?

42:40.725 --> 42:42.560
I want to become human
as soon as possible.

42:52.028 --> 42:54.572
Shut your mouth before I shut it for you.

42:56.616 --> 42:59.577
How dare you say that to me
wearing that face?

43:00.411 --> 43:03.331
- But sis--
- Don't call me that.

43:03.915 --> 43:06.584
I don't know who you were waiting for,
but it isn't me.

43:06.667 --> 43:09.587
I have no desire to help you in that way.

43:11.214 --> 43:12.131
But still…

43:12.215 --> 43:15.218
Whatever you choose to do with your life
has nothing to do with me.

43:15.301 --> 43:17.136
So leave me out of it.

43:17.220 --> 43:20.014
I can barely take care of myself as it is.

43:21.516 --> 43:23.059
Do you understand me?

43:25.186 --> 43:27.021
You're not the one I've been missing.

43:27.939 --> 43:31.150
So I don't need to feel
like I owe you anything.

43:32.026 --> 43:34.612
So don't ever show up
in front of me again.

43:36.280 --> 43:38.282
She seemed hurt,

43:38.366 --> 43:40.743
seeing how she left
without a word this morning.

43:42.411 --> 43:44.539
You don't seem
to understand the situation.

43:44.622 --> 43:46.541
We just got played.

43:46.624 --> 43:49.210
We came all this way,
suffered through hell,

43:49.293 --> 43:50.962
and now we're leaving empty-handed.

43:52.547 --> 43:54.257
I guess so, but…

43:56.509 --> 43:59.554
True, who am I to worry?
I'm a mess myself.

44:01.556 --> 44:02.723
So, what's the plan now?

44:02.807 --> 44:06.102
I'm going to go back
and dig through some old texts.

44:06.894 --> 44:08.938
"Old texts"? Like, ancient books?

44:09.021 --> 44:12.400
Yes, there are books on secret methods
for situations like this.

44:12.483 --> 44:14.819
Oh, really now?

44:16.612 --> 44:19.031
You don't remember any
off the top of your head?

44:20.491 --> 44:23.578
How would I remember something
I read centuries ago?

44:25.413 --> 44:28.791
Man, the international break
is coming up soon.

44:28.875 --> 44:30.585
I really need to switch back soon.

44:33.129 --> 44:36.048
Who cares about
some stupid ball game right now?

44:36.799 --> 44:38.509
It is important.

44:38.593 --> 44:40.803
It's an international match.
A game for the national team.

44:40.887 --> 44:44.015
Honestly, aren't you
a Korean nine-tailed fox?

44:44.098 --> 44:45.683
Where's your patriotism?

44:49.187 --> 44:51.898
I've been around longer than Korea has.

44:53.482 --> 44:57.236
Look, I don't know if you identify
with Joseon or Goryeo,

44:57.320 --> 45:00.239
but we're still one people.

45:03.201 --> 45:06.913
We are different species.

45:06.996 --> 45:09.081
Don't give me that "one people" crap.

45:10.041 --> 45:12.043
Come on, Ok-sun.

45:12.126 --> 45:13.628
What? I'm not Ok-sun.

45:15.338 --> 45:18.216
But I saw your ID at the police station.

45:18.299 --> 45:22.678
- Your name isn't Eun-ho. It's Kim Ok-sun.
- I told you, it's not Kim Ok-sun!

45:22.762 --> 45:27.058
- That damn old geezer just put whatever--
- That's just a typical grandma name.

45:27.141 --> 45:29.352
Why be embarrassed about it, Ok-sun?

45:30.519 --> 45:32.438
My grandma's name is Kim Bok-sun.

45:34.523 --> 45:37.818
I'm not embarrassed.
I'm telling you, Ok-sun is…

45:40.446 --> 45:43.574
My name is Eun-ho!

45:43.658 --> 45:46.869
All right, I'll just call you Eun-ho.

45:47.453 --> 45:48.955
- Ok-sun.
- Hey!

45:49.038 --> 45:51.916
Why are you yelling, Ok-sun?
You'll burst my eardrums.

45:51.999 --> 45:53.668
I'm not Ok-sun!

45:53.751 --> 45:56.212
All right, Eun-ho.
I'll call you Eun-ho, okay?

45:56.295 --> 45:58.381
- Ok-sun.
- It's Eun-ho!

45:58.965 --> 46:01.509
That damn old geezer, seriously.

46:05.972 --> 46:08.099
What is it, Si-yeol? What's wrong with it?

46:09.642 --> 46:10.685
We're out of gas.

46:12.019 --> 46:13.145
So put some in.

46:15.564 --> 46:20.111
Look, I was debating whether
to tell you this, but…

46:20.861 --> 46:21.737
What?

46:22.905 --> 46:24.490
My wallet's gone.

46:25.741 --> 46:27.535
- What?
- Listen.

46:28.411 --> 46:31.664
I think it fell out
when I rolled down the mountain.

46:34.333 --> 46:35.793
Then what do we do now?

46:53.477 --> 46:56.314
Hey, here comes one.

47:01.444 --> 47:03.863
What a rude bastard.

47:04.905 --> 47:08.367
When I turn back into a nine-tailed fox,
I'll catch him and just…

47:09.744 --> 47:13.080
We can't even call the insurance company
since my phone's dead.

47:17.084 --> 47:19.628
Si-yeol, let's just walk.

47:19.712 --> 47:20.796
What?

47:21.380 --> 47:23.632
Walk home? Do you know how far that is?

47:24.175 --> 47:26.761
Then are we just going
to stand here like this?

47:26.844 --> 47:28.471
Start walking.

47:30.806 --> 47:32.600
Look, we can't walk there.

47:32.683 --> 47:34.810
Why not?

47:35.311 --> 47:37.646
In the old days,
even frail little scholars

47:37.730 --> 47:40.232
crossed mountains and rivers
to take their exams.

47:41.525 --> 47:43.319
- Aren't you an athlete?
- Jeez.

47:43.819 --> 47:46.739
I'm not talking about me.
I'm talking about you.

47:46.822 --> 47:49.200
You can't use skills
like earth-folding anymore.

47:49.283 --> 47:50.242
Please.

47:51.077 --> 47:54.497
I've hiked Seoraksan Mountain twice
in this human body.

47:56.165 --> 47:57.541
We must be near Seoul anyway.

47:57.625 --> 47:59.168
It can't be much farther.

48:01.921 --> 48:03.381
I give up.

48:08.469 --> 48:11.389
So, what's your plan going forward?

48:12.556 --> 48:14.016
What do you mean?

48:14.517 --> 48:16.560
You're completely broke right now.

48:17.061 --> 48:20.147
In the human world,
you can't do a single thing without money.

48:20.231 --> 48:21.565
I don't know.

48:22.066 --> 48:24.485
It's not like
I'll be stuck this way forever.

48:25.069 --> 48:27.780
What about dinner tonight? And tomorrow?

48:28.614 --> 48:31.826
- Are you going to let me starve?
- I'm sure there's cash at home.

48:31.909 --> 48:34.203
I can't be completely broke.

48:35.079 --> 48:36.080
Wait a second.

48:36.872 --> 48:38.874
Don't you have a ton of money?

48:38.958 --> 48:39.917
What?

48:40.000 --> 48:43.212
Think about how much
you ripped me off just a few days ago.

48:43.295 --> 48:45.673
You couldn't have spent it all already.

48:45.756 --> 48:46.632
I still have it.

48:47.258 --> 48:48.467
There we go then.

48:49.218 --> 48:51.804
Let's just use that for now.

48:51.887 --> 48:55.099
I'll pay you back
once I switch back to my old life.

48:55.975 --> 48:58.394
- But it's at my house.
- Okay, let's go get it.

48:59.437 --> 49:03.023
Actually, we can just crash
at your place for a while.

49:03.566 --> 49:05.025
You saw the state of my place.

49:05.109 --> 49:07.027
Yours has to be better than that.

49:07.111 --> 49:09.029
Sorry, but we can't go to my house.

49:09.530 --> 49:11.866
My house is halfway up
Myohyangsan Mountain.

49:12.366 --> 49:14.452
Your house is halfway up a mountain?

49:15.161 --> 49:18.831
Then I guess we'll just grab the cash
and find another place to stay.

49:19.457 --> 49:21.542
I said, it's on Myohyangsan Mountain.

49:22.126 --> 49:23.544
Okay, so what?

49:24.211 --> 49:27.131
Is it really high up?
Higher than Seoraksan Mountain?

49:28.215 --> 49:30.551
Don't you know where
Myohyangsan Mountain is?

49:43.189 --> 49:44.732
GWANGHWAMUN

49:57.328 --> 49:58.454
THE CLEAR WATERS OF BAEKDU

50:06.629 --> 50:07.713
North Korea?

50:08.339 --> 50:09.882
Your house is in North Korea?

50:09.965 --> 50:11.300
Yes.

50:12.635 --> 50:14.803
Myohyangsan Mountain is in North Korea?

50:15.346 --> 50:17.056
And your house is hidden up there?

50:17.681 --> 50:18.766
You heard me.

50:19.767 --> 50:23.020
Why live there when there are
so many decent mountains around?

50:23.854 --> 50:25.397
I was born there.

50:25.481 --> 50:27.650
Myohyangsan Mountain
has always been my home.

50:28.692 --> 50:30.903
It's humans who put up
barbed wire wherever they pleased.

50:30.986 --> 50:32.363
Why take it out on me?

50:32.446 --> 50:34.782
But you make all your money in the South.

50:34.865 --> 50:36.951
Why didn't you just buy a house in Seoul?

50:37.034 --> 50:38.994
Did you forget I could use earth-folding?

50:39.078 --> 50:41.872
It's a dozen steps from home to Gangnam,
so why would I bother?

50:41.956 --> 50:43.666
You can't be serious!

50:46.710 --> 50:48.295
Seriously.

50:48.379 --> 50:50.172
Isn't there any other way?

50:50.881 --> 50:53.842
Right, what if we ask
that eight-tailed fox from yesterday?

50:53.926 --> 50:56.428
We could just ask her to go get the money.

50:58.347 --> 51:00.140
No one can find that place but me.

51:00.224 --> 51:01.308
I put up a barrier.

51:02.851 --> 51:05.813
A barrier painstakingly made
to evade the eyes of the deities.

51:05.896 --> 51:08.691
You think some dimwitted eight-tailed fox
could get through that?

51:08.774 --> 51:09.900
Give me a break.

51:10.401 --> 51:12.236
You're no help at all, ever.

51:14.613 --> 51:18.784
Gosh, Si-yeol.
How much longer do we have to walk?

51:18.867 --> 51:20.828
My legs are killing me.

51:21.370 --> 51:23.539
We haven't even been walking
for 30 minutes.

51:24.373 --> 51:25.958
We have another 12 hours to go.

51:26.041 --> 51:29.503
Jeez, this damn human body
is the absolute worst.

51:34.383 --> 51:36.510
What's going on?
Why does it sting so much?

51:37.136 --> 51:38.012
Be careful.

51:38.637 --> 51:42.099
Just because it's not summer
doesn't mean you can't get sunburned.

51:42.182 --> 51:44.143
We don't even have money for sunscreen.

51:59.491 --> 52:00.618
Si-yeol, look at this.

52:02.369 --> 52:04.288
Doesn't this work
just as well as sunscreen?

52:06.624 --> 52:09.209
Still, you look ridiculous.

52:10.085 --> 52:11.795
So you're not going to use it?

52:13.297 --> 52:15.591
All right, give it here. I'll hold it.

52:20.012 --> 52:22.181
See? Better than nothing, right?

52:22.264 --> 52:23.474
I guess so.

52:26.977 --> 52:28.812
Anyway, how much longer do we have to go?

52:28.896 --> 52:32.149
You just asked.
Now it's 11 hours and 59 minutes.

52:45.287 --> 52:46.413
What…

52:50.125 --> 52:51.835
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD
KANG SI-YEOL

52:51.919 --> 52:54.296
This guy…

52:57.341 --> 52:58.300
Is that you, sis?

52:59.927 --> 53:03.097
Is it really you? You came back?

53:20.572 --> 53:22.366
Are we there yet?

53:23.867 --> 53:24.785
Almost.

53:26.954 --> 53:29.540
Good thing we met
a decent human along the way.

53:30.040 --> 53:31.875
I seriously thought I was going to die.

53:32.668 --> 53:34.378
When I get back to normal,

53:34.461 --> 53:37.381
I'll have to bless that human
with a winning lottery ticket.

53:39.258 --> 53:40.384
That's a good idea.

53:41.427 --> 53:42.928
I wonder if he likes soccer.

53:43.011 --> 53:46.473
I was thinking of giving him
tickets to the Champions League final.

53:54.314 --> 53:55.190
I'm hungry.

54:02.823 --> 54:04.533
You know, come to think of it,

54:05.117 --> 54:08.495
you must've made connections
with quite a few humans over the years.

54:08.579 --> 54:11.874
People may have forgotten me,
but it's not the same for you.

54:12.833 --> 54:13.834
By any chance,

54:14.626 --> 54:16.211
isn't there anyone you can ask for help?

54:16.295 --> 54:17.254
There isn't.

54:17.337 --> 54:20.924
Why not? There must be people
whose wishes you granted.

54:21.008 --> 54:22.593
You said you hand-pick your clients.

54:22.676 --> 54:24.762
Aren't they all as rich as I am?

54:24.845 --> 54:28.223
They're rich.
They've got both money and power.

54:28.307 --> 54:31.602
So? Let's go ask them for help.

54:31.685 --> 54:33.729
We can pay them back double later.

54:37.524 --> 54:39.151
I've felt this for a while,

54:39.777 --> 54:42.362
but for a human, you sure seem clueless
about your own kind.

54:42.446 --> 54:44.281
Like how you blindly trusted your friend.

54:45.908 --> 54:47.326
What are you trying to say now?

54:47.409 --> 54:49.828
I never trust humans.

54:49.912 --> 54:52.372
Especially the ones with money and power.

54:52.456 --> 54:55.375
You know why they grovel
and suck up to me?

54:55.876 --> 54:58.086
It's only because I have power.

55:00.672 --> 55:02.800
If they find out I've lost my power,

55:03.300 --> 55:05.260
they'll try to get back at me somehow.

55:06.094 --> 55:11.350
Humans forget favors quickly
but hold on to grudges forever.

55:11.975 --> 55:13.977
Come on, surely not all of them?

55:14.603 --> 55:17.689
There must be some
you're on good terms with.

55:18.899 --> 55:20.651
Do you really think so?

55:22.778 --> 55:25.072
I guess not.

55:25.697 --> 55:29.409
You probably bullied them
the same way you did me.

55:29.493 --> 55:30.953
I tamed them.

55:31.912 --> 55:33.330
So they're easier to handle.

55:34.957 --> 55:38.752
Anyway, I have to be more careful
with those who know who I am.

55:38.836 --> 55:41.255
So watch your mouth, got it?

55:42.798 --> 55:45.300
That's why you should've been
a little nicer all along.

55:47.052 --> 55:48.136
What?

55:49.513 --> 55:50.764
I said I'm hungry.

55:52.975 --> 55:53.934
Jeez.

55:54.017 --> 55:56.228
Seriously, what is going on?

55:56.311 --> 55:58.981
Why isn't Si-yeol at home
or picking up his phone?

55:59.481 --> 56:00.816
Tell me about it.

56:00.899 --> 56:04.111
How can he borrow a car
and then ghost us for two days?

56:04.611 --> 56:06.905
You don't think something happened
to Si-yeol, do you?

56:06.989 --> 56:08.156
No way.

56:08.240 --> 56:09.992
I'm the one with the problem, damn it.

56:10.075 --> 56:11.952
I've got early morning
deliveries but no car.

56:13.245 --> 56:16.582
You can take my car again today.

56:16.665 --> 56:18.917
Your car is so embarrassing to drive.

56:19.001 --> 56:21.086
Everyone stares at it.

56:21.837 --> 56:23.881
Jeong-bae has a nice car.
Why are you embarrassed?

56:23.964 --> 56:25.382
That's why it's embarrassing.

56:25.465 --> 56:28.760
If it were just an expensive car,
I wouldn't be complaining.

56:28.844 --> 56:32.222
But who drives a supercar
for an early morning delivery gig?

56:32.306 --> 56:34.600
Plus, the gas mileage just sucks.

56:34.683 --> 56:37.352
After paying for gas,
I make basically nothing.

56:37.436 --> 56:40.647
But you know
my baby only takes premium, right?

56:40.731 --> 56:43.442
I know, you jerk. Jeez!

56:44.484 --> 56:47.487
But seriously,
don't you find that car uncomfortable?

56:47.571 --> 56:49.740
What kind of car doesn't have a back seat?

56:50.449 --> 56:55.537
Right? It costs a fortune,
but it's only half a car.

56:55.621 --> 56:57.039
It's only got two doors too.

56:57.122 --> 56:58.790
You rich kids…

56:58.874 --> 57:00.334
Hey, take a look at this.

57:08.091 --> 57:10.469
It hit the upper limit twice.
Just look at this stock.

57:10.552 --> 57:12.512
It's going to bottom out,
then bounce back.

57:12.596 --> 57:15.515
Just tell your grandma
to invest a little until then.

57:17.935 --> 57:19.394
Thank you.

57:20.771 --> 57:21.813
For now,

57:23.231 --> 57:24.816
let's go inside and get some rest.

57:24.900 --> 57:25.984
- Okay.
- Yeah.

57:38.580 --> 57:39.498
Woo-seok.

57:44.169 --> 57:45.045
I'm sorry.

57:46.129 --> 57:47.339
It took me so long.

57:48.131 --> 57:51.343
Wait, how are you even here?

57:51.426 --> 57:54.513
He probably ran his ass off in a panic.

57:57.975 --> 57:59.518
I see you were together.

57:59.601 --> 58:02.020
Why? Does that make you twice as nervous?

58:02.521 --> 58:04.606
Seeing me next to Si-yeol?

58:09.319 --> 58:10.362
Si-yeol.

58:10.904 --> 58:14.825
I was blinded by greed and crossed a line.

58:16.118 --> 58:18.370
I should've asked you face-to-face.

58:21.456 --> 58:22.457
Honestly,

58:23.625 --> 58:25.711
these past few days felt like a dream.

58:28.213 --> 58:32.759
The life I never even dared to dream of
became mine in an instant.

58:33.427 --> 58:34.761
- Woo-seok--
- I know.

58:34.845 --> 58:37.180
It's all yours. It's your life.

58:38.015 --> 58:39.224
I know I shouldn't be

58:40.183 --> 58:41.977
doing this to you.

58:42.060 --> 58:44.229
But just for one week.

58:44.980 --> 58:47.983
If a month is too long, how about a week?

58:48.066 --> 58:50.360
Let me play just one
international match next week.

58:50.444 --> 58:51.528
Do whatever you want.

58:54.781 --> 58:55.866
What?

58:55.949 --> 58:57.617
It's not like we'll stay switched forever.

58:57.701 --> 58:59.828
Spending a few days in your life…

59:01.329 --> 59:02.372
wasn't so bad.

59:03.290 --> 59:05.375
I've never had a chance to properly rest.

59:05.459 --> 59:07.169
I'll just think of it as a break.

59:08.879 --> 59:11.506
Really? You mean it?

59:11.590 --> 59:14.885
Let's keep it like this for now.
That way, you won't have any regrets.

59:14.968 --> 59:17.888
But when I say we need to switch,
we switch right away.

59:17.971 --> 59:19.765
You can promise me that, right?

59:20.849 --> 59:22.976
Yes, of course.

59:24.352 --> 59:25.645
Thank you, Si-yeol.

59:29.357 --> 59:32.110
I seriously won't forget this favor.

59:33.737 --> 59:36.656
Sis, I found a way!

59:37.282 --> 59:38.742
It's going to take some time,

59:38.825 --> 59:41.578
but I found a way for you to turn back

59:41.661 --> 59:43.121
into a nine-tailed fox.

59:43.205 --> 59:45.999
Okay, let's talk about it later.

59:46.083 --> 59:48.919
That means he can
go back to his life too, right?

59:49.002 --> 59:50.337
Right?

01:00:28.708 --> 01:00:31.628
NO TAIL TO TELL

01:00:31.711 --> 01:00:33.088
You found a way?

01:00:33.171 --> 01:00:34.965
What if I become a nine-tailed fox?

01:00:35.048 --> 01:00:37.175
Then I'll have powers too,

01:00:37.259 --> 01:00:39.177
so we can just switch our fates.

01:00:39.261 --> 01:00:42.180
I think I should meet this Hyeon Woo-seok.

01:00:42.264 --> 01:00:45.016
You've invited quite the ghost in.

01:00:45.100 --> 01:00:47.227
So there's a chance we can't switch back

01:00:47.310 --> 01:00:49.104
if that method doesn't work?

01:00:49.187 --> 01:00:52.232
So doing good deeds
builds up spiritual power, right?

01:00:52.315 --> 01:00:54.401
But how long will that take?

01:00:54.484 --> 01:00:56.945
- Usually, it takes about 100 years.
- A hundred years?

01:00:57.028 --> 01:00:58.071
Brace yourself.

01:00:58.697 --> 01:01:01.199
We'll be slammed starting tomorrow.

01:01:03.660 --> 01:01:05.579
Subtitle translation by Susanna Kim
